<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 May, from 1360 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bretigny" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bretigny.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1360">1360 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">666 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward III and John II agree the Treaty of Brétigny</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a> and the captive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-france">John II of France</a> agreed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bretigny">Treaty of Brétigny</a>, ending the first phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. Edward gave up his claim to the French crown for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over Aquitaine, Calais and Ponthieu.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bretigny">Treaty of Brétigny</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1429">1429 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">597 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc helps lift the English siege of Orléans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French forces inspired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> ended the English siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, a turning point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. The French regained the initiative, and Joan brought Charles VII to his coronation at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1559">1559 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">467 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth I's Act of Supremacy receives royal assent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Act restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-england">Church of England</a>'s independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and made Elizabeth its Supreme Governor. With the Act of Uniformity it formed the basis of the Elizabethan religious settlement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1794">1794 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chemist Antoine Lavoisier is guillotined in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lavoisier, executed as a former tax farmer during the Terror, had named oxygen and hydrogen and set chemistry on modern foundations. 'It took them only an instant to cut off that head,' said Lagrange.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1846">1846 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">180 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US and Mexican armies clash at Palo Alto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Zachary Taylor's artillery won the first major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican-American War</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a>. By 1848 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> had lost about half its territory, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1886">1886 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Coca-Cola goes on sale at an Atlanta pharmacy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pharmacist John Pemberton's new syrup, mixed with carbonated water, was sold at Jacobs' Pharmacy for five cents a glass. It became one of the most widely recognised brands in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allies celebrate Victory in Europe Day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s surrender took effect and crowds filled the streets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, where the surrender came after midnight, victory is marked on 9 May.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Troops fire on Buddhist protesters in Huế</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">South Vietnamese forces fired on crowds protesting a ban on Buddhist flags, killing nine. The Buddhist crisis that followed undermined President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-dinh-diem">Ngo Dinh Diem</a>, who was overthrown in November.</p></div></li></ol>
