<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 8 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-iv-of-styria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ottokar-iv-of-styria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ottokar IV of Styria</span><span class="tp">1163–1192</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-bey-al-kabir"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-bey-al-kabir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ali Bey al-Kabir</span><span class="tp">1728–1773</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kamehameha-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kamehameha I</span><span class="tp">c. 1758–1819</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paul-gauguin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paul-gauguin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paul Gauguin</span><span class="tp">1848–1903</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/josef-terboven"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Josef Terboven</span><span class="tp">1898–1945</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
